  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the child as embodying urgent desire",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual entity 'child' (the young boy) because the meme uses the child's determined expression and raised fist to symbolize the user's own impatience or urgent desire for something. The child becomes a stand-in for the viewer, who is imagining themselves in the role of the demanding child. This projection is implicit, not explicit, but it is a core function of the meme format — the viewer identifies with the child's behavior and emotion. The textual elements 'i want it' and 'now is a good time' reinforce this projection by directly stating the desire, which the user then maps onto themselves via the child's visual representation.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
